 the certified-op grace'; Summary: 'run_http_with_grace must not couple uvicorn's timeout_graceful_shutdown to the certified-op drain grace'","src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py:102 signature already has `uvicorn_graceful_seconds: float = DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS`; line 143 `timeout_graceful_shutdown=int(uvicorn_graceful_seconds)`","src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:53 `DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS = 10` docstring: 'deliberately DECOUPLED from DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS (bug 2f46)'","src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py:85-92 `_on_sigterm` already calls `gauge.begin_draining()` then `drain_then_exit(...)` then `setattr(server, 'should_exit', True)` — exactly AC3","src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py:41-57 `drain_then_exit` already returns immediately for idle gauges and is bounded by `grace_seconds` for busy ones — AC2","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py:498 `test_run_http_with_grace_decouples_uvicorn_grace_from_op_grace_2f46` asserts `tgs != 1200` and `tgs == int(health.DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS)` — AC1 & AC4 already proven","src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py:8 docstring: 'extracted so _mcp_health stays under the 800-LOC module cap AFTER the bug-2f46 fast-drain fix' (past tense — fix already landed)"],"finding":"The plan's central premise — that `run_http_with_grace` couples uvicorn's `timeout_graceful_shutdown` to the certified-op drain grace so 'mcp retirement always burns the full 1200s drain' — is refuted by the committed code. src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py already passes `timeout_graceful_shutdown=int(uvicorn_graceful_seconds)` using a separate parameter defaulting to `DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS = 10`, explicitly decoupled from `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS = 1200`. The bug-2f46 fix this plan proposes appears already landed, including the SIGTERM handler ordering (begin_draining -> drain_then_exit -> should_exit) and its tests.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f387ebe6102c8f580","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan title + Summary + all Ac